              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Case: 3:24-cr-00008-DCR-MAS Doc #: 79 Filed: 03/27/25 Page: 1 of 8 -\nEastern Page\nDistrict of Kentucky\nID#: 391\nAO 24513 (Rev. 09/19) Judgment in a Criminal Case FILED\nSheet I\n\nMar - 27 2025\nUNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT Robert R. Carr\nEastern District of Kentucky- Central Division at Frankfo1t Clerk, U.S. District Court\n\n)\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA ) JUDGMENT IN A CRIMINAL CASE\nv. )\n)\nAustin David Stafford ) Case Number: 3:24-CR-008-DCR-0 I\n) USM Number: 69549-510\n)\n) John C. Helmuth\n) Defendant's Attorney\nTHE DEFENDANT:\nl8l pleaded guilty to count(s) 1 [DE #1]\n-~-~----------------------------------\n\u25a1 pleaded nolo contendere to count(s)\nwhich was accepted by the court.\nD was found guilty on count(s)\nafter a plea of not guilty.\n\nThe defendant is adjudicated guilty of these offenses:\n\nTitle & Section Nature of OITense Offense Ended Count\n18:225 l(a) Employing, Using, Persuading, Inducing, Enticing, and Coercing a Minor to Engage June I 0, 2022 I\nin Sexually Explicit Conduct for the Purpose of Producing a Visual Depiction of that\nConduct\n\nThe defendant is sentenced as provided in pages 2 through\nthe Sentencing Reform Act of 1984.\n- -8- - of this judgment. The sentence is imposed pursuant to\nD The defendant has been found not guilty on count(s)\nl8l Count(s) 2 and 4 [DE #I] D is IZl are dismissed on !he motion of the United States.\n\nIt is ordered that the defendant must notilY the United States attorney for this district within 30 days of any change of name, residence,\nor mailing address until all fines, restitution, costs, and special assessments imposed by this judgment are fully paid. If ordered to pay restitution,\nthe defendant must notify the cou11 and United States attorney of material changes in economic circumstances.\n\nNOTICE HEREBY GIVEN OF THE ENTRY\nOF THIS ORDER OR JUDGMENT\nON _______________________\nMar - 27 2025 Honorable Danny C. Reeves, U.S. District Judge\nROBERT R. CARR, CLERK Name and Title ofJudge\nBY ________________________\nMYounce DC\nMarch 27, 2025\nDate\nCase: 3:24-cr-00008-DCR-MAS Doc #: 79 Filed: 03/27/25 Page: 2 of 8 - Page\nID#: 392\nAO 245B (Rev. 09/19) Judgment ina Criminal Case\n\nJudgment - l'agc __2__ of\nDEFENDANT: Austin David Stafford\nCASE NUMBER: 3:24-CR-008-DCR-0 1\n\nIMPRISONMENT\n\nThe defendant is hereby committed to the custody of the Federal Bureau of Prisons to be imprisoned for a total term of:\n\nTHREE HUNDRED SIXTY (360) MONTHS\n\nIE.l The court makes the following recommendations to the Bureau of Prisons:\nThat the defendant participate in a sex offender treatment program.\nThal the defendant receive a mental health evaluation and any necessary follow-up treatment.\nThat the defendant receive a medical evaluation ,md any necessary treatment.\nThat the defendant be designated to FMC Butner.\n\n~ The defend,mt is remanded to the custody of the United States Marshal.\n\n\u25a1 The defendant shall surrender to the United States Marshal for this district:\n\u25a1\n\u25a1 at\n- - - - - - - - \u25a1 a.m. p.m. on\n0 as notified by the United States Marshal.\n\n\u25a1 The defendant shall surrender for service of sentence at the institution designated by the Bureau of Prisons:\n\u25a1 before 2 p.m. on\n\u25a1 as notified by the United States Marshal.\n0 as notified by lhe Probation or Pretrial Services Office.\n\nRETURN\n\nI have executed this judgment as follows:\n\nDefendant delivered on to\n\n_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ , with a certified copy of this judgment\n\nUNITED STATES MARSHAL\n\nBy\nDEPUTY UNITED STATES MARSHAL\nCase: 3:24-cr-00008-DCR-MAS Doc #: 79 Filed: 03/27/25 Page: 3 of 8 - Page\nID#: 393\nAO 2450 (Rev. 09/19) Judgment in a Criminal Case\n\nJudgment-Page --'J__ of 8\nDEFENDANT: Austin David Stafford\nCASE NUMBER: 3:24-CR-00B~DCR-O 1\n\nSUPERVISED RELEASE\nUpon release from imprisonment, you will be on supervised release for a term of:\nTHIRTY (30) YEARS\n\nTo run concurrently with the term of supervised release imposed in U.S. Dist1\u00b7ict Com't,\nli:.11stern District of Kentucky, Docket Number 5:23-CR-067-DCR-01\n\nMANDATORY CONDITIONS\n\nI. You must not commit another federal. state or local crime.\n2. You must not unlawfully possess a controlled substance.\n3. You must refrain from any unlawful use of a controlled substance. You must submit to one drug test within 15 days of release from\nimprisonment and at least two periodic drug tests thereafter, as determined by the court.\n\u25a1 The above drug testing condition is sus1Jended, based on the court's determination that you\npose a low risk of future substance abuse. (Check. ifapplirobleJ\n4. \u25a1 You must make restitution in accordance with 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 3663 and 3663A or any other statute authorizing a sentence of\nrestitution. (Check, ifappflcflble .)\n5. ~ You must cooperate in the collection of DNA as directed by the probation officer. (Chrek, ifap\u00b5ficable.)\n6. \u25a1 Yon must comply with the requirements of the Sex Offender Registration and Notific11tion Act (34 U.S.C. \u00a7 20901 \u25ba et seq.) as\ndirected by the probation officer, the Bureau of Prisons, or any state sex offender registration agency in the location where you\nreside, work, are a student, or were convicted ofa qualifying offense. (Check, ifap\u00b5ficable.}\n1. \u25a1 You must participate in fill npproved program for domestic violence, (CltecJ.:, ffapplicable}\n\nYon must comply with the standard conditions that have been adopted by this court as well as with any other conditions on the attached\npage.\nCase: 3:24-cr-00008-DCR-MAS Doc #: 79 Filed: 03/27/25 Page: 4 of 8 - Page\nID#: 394\nAO 2458 (Rev, 09/ 19) Judgment in II Crimimtl Case\nSheet JA - Release\n\nJudgment--Page 4 of\nDEFENDANT: Austin David Stafford\nCASE NUMBER: 3:24-CR-008-DCR-O I\n\nSTANDARD CONDITIONS OF SUPERVISION\n\nAs part of your supervised release, you must comp]y with the following standard conditions of supervision. These condilions are imposed\nbecause they establish the basic expectations for your behavior while on supervision and identify the minimum tools needed IJy probation\nofficers to keep informed, report to the court about, and bring about improvements in your conduct and condilion.\nl. You must report to the probation oflice ht the federaljudkial district where you are authorized to reside within 72 hours of your\nrelease from imprisonment, unless the probation officer instructs you to report to a different probation office or within a different time\nframe_\n2. After initially reporting to the 1noblllion office, you will receive instructions from the court or the probation officer about how and\nwhen you must report to the probation officer, and you must report to the probation officer as instructed.\n3. You must not knowingly leave the federal judicial district where you are authorized to reside without first getting permission from the\ncourt or the probation officer.\n4. You must ans\\ver truthfully the questions asked IJy yoor probation officer.\n5. You must live al a place approved by the probation officer. If you plan to change where you live or anything about your living\narrangements (such as the people you live with), you must notify the probation officer at least 10 days IJefore the change. If notifying\nthe probation officer in advance is not possible due to unan1ici1mted circumstances, you must notify the probation oflicer within 72\nhours of becoming aware ofa change or expected change.\n6_ You must allow the probation officer to visit you at any time at your borne or elsewhere, and you must permit the probation officer to\ntake any items prohibited by the conditions of your supervision that he or she observes in plain view.\n7. You must work full time (at least 30 hours per week) at a lawful type of employment, unless the probation oft1cer excuses you from\ndoing so. If you do not have full-rime employment you must try to find ftdl~time employment, unless the probation officer excuses\nyou from doing so. If you plan to change where you work or anything about your work (such as your position or your job\nresponsibilities), you must notify the probation officer at least lO days before the change. If notifying the probation officer at least 10\ndays in advance is not possible due to unanticipated circumstances, you must notify the probation officer within 72 hours of becoming\naware ofa change or expected change.\n8. You must not communicate or internet with someone you know is engaged in criminal activity. lfyou know someone has been\nconvicted of a felony, you must not knowingly communicate or interact with that person without first getting the permission of the\nprobation officer.\n9. If you are arreste-0 or questioned by a law enforcement officer, you must notify the prolJation officer within 72 hours.\n10. You must not own, possess, or have access to a firem\u00b7m, ammunition, destructive device, or dangerous weapon (i.e., anything that was\ndesigned, or was modified for, the specific purpose of causing bodily injury or death to another person such as nunchakus or tasers ).\n11. You must not act or make any agreement with a law enforcement agency to act as a confidential human source or informant without\nfirst getting the permission of the court.\nI 2. If the probation officer determines that you pose a risk to another person (including an organization), the probation officer may\nrequire you to notify the person about the risk and you must comply with that instruction. The probation officer may contact the\nperson and confirm that you have notified the person about the risk.\n13_ You must follow the instructions of the probation officer related to the conditions of supervision.\n14. You must comply strictly with the orders of your physicians or other prescribing source with respect to the use of any prescribed\ncontrolled substances. You must report any changes reg8rding your prescriptions to your probation officer immediately (i.e., no later\nthan 72 hours). The prolJation officer may verify your prescriptions and your compliance with this paragraph.\n\nU.S. Probation Office Use Only\n\nA U.S. probation officer has instructed me on the conditions specified IJy the court and has provided me with a written copy of this\njudgment containing these conditions. For further information regarding these conditions, see Oi\u2022en\u2022iew of Probarion and Superi\u2022ised\nRelease Conditions, available at: www.uscourts,gov.\n\nDefendant's Signature Date _____________\nCase: 3:24-cr-00008-DCR-MAS Doc #: 79 Filed: 03/27/25 Page: 5 of 8 - Page\nID#: 395\nAO 245B (Rev. 09119) Judgment in a Criminal Case\n\nof 8\nDEFENDANT: Austin David Stafford\nCASE NUMBER: 3:24-CR-0 08-DCR~O 1\n\nSPECIAL CONDITIONS OF SUPERVISION\n1. You may not use or consume alcohol,\n\n2. You must participate in a substance abuse treatment program and follow the rules and regulations of that program\nat the direction and discretion of the United States Probation Office. You are required to attend sessio11s, and you\nmust pay aU or a portion of the cost of the treatment services provided pursuant to General Order 22-09. The United\nStates Probation Office is responsible for supervising your participation in the program.\n\n3. You may not possess, use, or consume marijuana or marijuana products.\n\n4. You: (i) must pat1icipate in a program for treatment of mental health/sexual disorders; must undergo a sex olfender\nrisk assessment, psychosexual evaluation and any other evaluations as needed; (ii) will be subject to periodic\npolygraph examinations, Computer Voice Stress Analysis (CVSA) testing and any other psychological and\nphysiological testing, at the discretion and direction of the United States Probation Office; and (iii) must follow the\nrules and regulations of the sex offender treatment program as implemented by the United States Probation Office\nin this district.\n\n5. Your residence and employment must be pre-approved by the United States Probation Office and in compliance\nwith state and local law.\n\n6. You may not: (i) frequent, volunteer, or work at p}aces where childl'en under the age of 18 congregate; or (ii) have\nany contact with the identified victims.\n\n7. You may not associate or have verbal, written, telephonic, or electronic communication with any person under the\nage of 18 without permission from the United States Probation Office. This prohibition does not include persons\nunder the age of 18 with whom you must deal to obtain ordinary and usual commercial services.\n\n8. You may not (i) view or possess any \"visual depiction\" (as defined in l 8 U.S.C. \u00a72256) including any photograph,\nfilm, video, picture, or computer or computer-generated image or picture, whether made or produced by electronic,\nmechanical, or other means, of \"sexually explicit conduct\" (as defined in 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2256) or that would\ncompromise your treatment; or (ii) enter any location where such materials, sexually stimulating performances, or\nsexually oriented materials, items or services are available.\n\n9. You may not: (i) possess any materials depicting or describing \"child pornography\" or \"simulated child\npornography\" as defined in 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2256 or that would compromise your sex offender treatment.; or (ii) enter\nany location where such materials may be accessed, obtained or viewed, including pictures, photographs, books,\nwritings, drawings, videos or video games.\n\nIO. You must comply with the requirements of the Sex Oftender Registration and Notification Act (42 U.S.C. \u00a7 16901;\net seq.) as directed by the United States Probation Office, the Bureau of Prisons, or any state sex offender registration\nagency in which you reside, work, are a student, or were convicted of a qualifying offense.\n\nI J. You may not possess or use a computer or any electronic device with access to any onftline computer service at any\nlocation (including place of employment) without receiving the written approval of the United States Probation\nOffice in advance. This includes any Internet Service provider, bulletin board system, or any other public or private\nnetwork or e-mail system.\nCase: 3:24-cr-00008-DCR-MAS Doc #: 79 Filed: 03/27/25 Page: 6 of 8 - Page\nID#: 396\nAO 245D (Rev, 09/19) Judgme11t in o Criminal Case\n\nJudgment-Pagel __6__ of\nDEFENDANT: Austin David Stafford\nCASE NUMBER: 3:24-CR-008-DCR-01\n\nADDITIONAL SPECIAL CONDITIONS OF SUPERVISION\n\n12. You must consent to (i) the United States Probation Office conducting unannounced examinations of all electronic\ndevices, which may include retrieval and copying of ail memory from hardware/software and removal of such\nsystem(s) for the purpose of conducting a more thorough inspection; and (ii) having installed on yom computer(s)\nor electronic devices any hardware/software to monitor device use or pl'event access to particular materials, and to\nconsent to periodic inspection of any such installed hardware/software to insure it ls functioning properly.\n\n13. You must provide the United States Probation Office with accurate information about any computer system\n(hardware/software) or any electronic devices which you are allowed to possess or use; all account usernamcs; all\npasswords used by you; and you must abide by an rules of the Electronic Device Restriction and Monitoring\nProgram.\n\n14. You must submit your person, offices, properties, homes, residences, vehicles, storage units, papers, computers,\nother electronic devices, cloud storage locations, and data storage locations to a search conducted by the United\nStates Probation Office. Failure to submit to a search is grounds for revocation of supetvision. You must warn all\noccupants that the premises is subject to search according to this condition.\n\n15. You must provide the United States Probation Office with access to any requested financial information.\nCase: 3:24-cr-00008-DCR-MAS Doc #: 79 Filed: 03/27/25 Page: 7 of 8 - Page\nID#: 397\nAO 24SB {Rev. 09/19) Judgmrnt in a Criminal Case\n\nJudgment Page __7;........._ of B\nDEFENDANT: Austin David Stafford\nCASE NUMBER: 3:24-CR-008-DCR-O I\n\nCRIMINAL MONETARY PENALTIES\n\nThe defendant must pay the total criminal monetary penalties under the schedule of payme11ts on Sheet 6.\n\nAssessment Restitution fil!!.\u00a3 AV AA Assessment* JVTA Assessment**\nTOTALS $ 0.00 $ Waived $ NIA\n$ 100.00 $ NIA\n\nD The determination of restitution is deferred until An Amended J11dgmef1l in a Criminal Case (AO UJC) will be entered\nafter sucb determination.\n\u25a1 The defendant must make restitution (including community restitution) to the following pnyees in the amount listed below.\n\nIf the defendant makes a partial payment, each payee shall receive an approximately proportioned payment, unless specified otherwise in\nthe priority order or percentage payment column below. However, pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3664(i), all nonfederal victims must be paid\nbefore the United States is paid.\n\nName of Payee Total Loss*** Restit111io11 Ordered Priority or Perceolnge\n\nTOTALS $~-------\n\nD Restitution amount ordered pursuant to plea agreement S\nD The defendant must pay interest on restitution and a fine of more than $2,500, unless the restitution or fine is paid in full before the\nfifteenth day after the date of the judgment, pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3612(t). All of the payment options on Sheet 6 may be sobject\nto penalties for delinquency and default, pursuant to l 8 U.S.C. \u00a7 36 I2(g).\n\nD The court determined that the defendant does 1101 have the ability lo pay interest and it is ordered that:\n\u25a1 the interest requirement is waived for the D fine \u25a1 restitution.\n\u25a1 the interest requirement for the \u25a1 fine \u25a1 restitution is modified as follows:\n\n* Amy, Vicky, and Andy Child Pornography Victim Assistance Act of 2018, Pub. L. No. I )5-299.\n** Justice for Victims of Trafficking Act of20J 5, Pub. L. No. 114~22.\n**\"' Findings for the total amount of losses are required under Chapters l09A, 110, I lOA, and l 13A of Title 18 for offenses committed on or\nafter September 13, 1994, but before April 23, 1996.\nCase: 3:24-cr-00008-DCR-MAS Doc #: 79 Filed: 03/27/25 Page: 8 of 8 - Page\nID#: 398\nAO 245B (Rev. 09/19) Judgment in a Criminal Case\n\nJudgment- Page _ _8 __ of\nDEFENDANT: Austin David Stafford\nCASE NUMBER: 3:24-CR-008-DCR-O l\n\nSCHEDULE OF PAYMENTS\n\nHaving assessed the defendant's ability to pay, payment of the total criminal monetary penalties is due as follows:\n\nA 1:81 Lump sum payment of$ 100.00 due immediately, balance due\n\nn not fater than , or\nl.xl in accordance with \u25a1 C, \u25a1 D, \u25a1 E, or [l,;J F below; or\n\nB \u25a1 Payment to begin immediately (may be combined with \u25a1 C, [} D, or \u25a1 F below); or\n\nC D Payment in equal _ _ _ _ _ _ (e.g.. weekly, monthly, quarter/;~ installments of $ _ _ _ _ _ _ over a period of\n(e.g.. mo111h.s or years), to commence _ _ _ _ _ (e.g.. 30 or 60 days) after the date of this judgment; or\n\nD D Payment in equal _ _ _ _ _ _ (e.g., weekly, mo111hl;,. qimrterly) installments of $ _ _ _ _ _ _ over a period of\n(e.g.. monlhs or years), to commence _ _ _ _ _ (e.g., 30 or 60 days) after release from hnprisomnent to a\nterm of supervision; or\n\nE \u25a1 Payment during the term of supervised release will commence within _ _ _ _ _ (e.g., 30 or 60 days) after release from\nimprisonment. The court will set the payment plan based on an assessment of the defendant's ability to pay at that time; or\n\nF [:8,1 Special instructions regarding the payment of criminal monetary penalties:\n\nCriminal monetary penalties are payable to:\nClerk, U.S. District Court, Eastern District of Kentucky\n313 John C. Watts Federal Building) 330 West Broadway. Frankfort, KY 4060 I\n\nINCLUDE CASE NUMBER WITH ALL CORRESPONDENCE\n\nUnless the court has expressly ordered otherwise, if this judgment imposes imprisonment, pnyment of criminal monelary penalties is due during\nthe period ofimprisonment All criminal monetary penalties, except those payments mude through the Federal Bureau of Prisons' lnnmte fimmcin1\nResponsibility Program, arc made to the clerk of the court\n\nThe defendant shall receive credit for all payments previously made toward any criminal monetary penalties imposed,\n\n\u25a1 Joint and Several\n\nCase Number\nDefendant and Co-Defendant Names\n{including defendant ,mmber) Total Amount Joint and Several Amount Corresponding Payee. ifappmpriatQ\n\nD The defendant shall pay the cost of prosecution.\n\nD The defendant shall pay the following court cost(s):\n\n~ The detendant shall forfeit the defendant's interest in the following property to the United States:\nThe items listed in the Porfeiture Allegation of the Indictment, to wit;\na) UMX smartphone, UMX U693CL, bearing serial nmnber 69CL7012 l043632; b) Maxwest smartphone, IMEi I: 3546551 !0006478,\nIMEl2: [redacted-number], bearing serial number NTO5P20040000324; c) Motorola Moto E6 smartphone, XT2005DL; d) Lenovo\nThinkpad I IE Chromebook, bearing serial number LR-03 RD3F; and e) MOTO ES cellphone XT2005DL, IMEi: [redacted-number].\n\nPayments shall be applied in the followjng order: (I) assessment, (2) restitution principal, (3) restitution interest, (4) AVAA assessment,\n(5) fine principal, (6) fine interest, (7) community restitution, (8) JVT A assessment, (9) penalties, and ( 10) costs, including cost of\nprosecution and court costs."
